details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two rustic, halved sweet potatoes centered on individual matte ceramic plates, captured from a 3/4 overhead angle (40-degree) to ensure the full depth of the stuffing is visible. The foreground plate is in sharp focus, while the second plate sits slightly behind, softly blurred by the shallow depth of field. Each potato is split open, with the golden-orange, steaming-soft flesh acting as a base for a generous heap of dark green, wilted spinach and brown, tender lentils. A creamy, thick lemon-yogurt sauce is drizzled artistically over the center, topped with ivory-white crumbles of feta cheese and toasted, rough-chopped walnuts. The scene is lit by soft, natural light from a window on the left, casting subtle shadows and highlighting the glistening sheen of the yogurt and oil. The potatoes are set upon a worn, dark oak wood table showing authentic grain and small, realistic scratches. Props include a wooden spoon resting casually beside one plate and a crumpled linen napkin tucked partially beneath the dish. Scattered on the surface are a few loose walnut fragments and a small smear of yogurt. NO chickpeas, NO fresh parsley, NO fresh herbs. The colors are earthy: amber-gold potatoes, deep forest-green spinach, and cream-colored yogurt. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small yogurt drip on the plate rim, slightly uneven browning on the potato skins. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a crumb trail on the surface, a slight oil mark near the plate. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
  }
]
